<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alqas Mirza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1516–1550</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alqas Mirza was a Safavid prince, son of Shah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-i">Ismail I</a> and brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tahmasp-i">Shah Tahmasp I</a>. In 1538 he led the army that annexed Shirvan to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid Empire</a> and became its governor. He rebelled against Tahmasp in 1547, fled to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> and joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suleiman-the-magnificent">Suleiman the Magnificent</a>'s campaign against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> in 1548, but was captured in 1549 and died in prison the following year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alqas-mirza.jpg" alt="Alqas Mirza" width="320" height="584" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Istanbul,_Topkapi_Palace_Museum_MS_Hazine_1517_fol_471v_S%C3%BCleymanname_Elkas_Mirza_Suleiman_I_cropped_cropped.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
